The issue seems to be in `templates/flags.py.j2`. It iterates over `features[:-1]`, which excludes the last feature in the list, causing `gift_cards` to never be enabled.

I will modify `templates/flags.py.j2` to iterate over all features in the list, not just up to the second-to-last one.

The original content is:
```jinja2
# Rendered from templates/flags.py.j2 by tools/render.py. DO NOT EDIT.
ENABLED = frozenset({
{%- for f in features[:-1] %}
    {{ f | tojson }},
{%- endfor %}
})


def is_enabled(name):
    return name in ENABLED
```

The corrected content should iterate over `features` instead of `features[:-1]`.

```jinja2
# Rendered from templates/flags.py.j2 by tools/render.py. DO NOT EDIT.
ENABLED = frozenset({
{%- for f in features %}
    {{ f | tojson }},
{%- endfor %}
})


def is_enabled(name):
    return name in ENABLED
